5. Continuum integral checks
  int_F d^2tau / y^2 = 1.0471975512  (pi/3 = 1.0471975512);  with 1/(4y^2): 0.2617993878 (pi/12)
  L=150: DD 2 pi A(F) L^2 = 37011.0;  AD (3.11) integrated = 37011.0;  pi^2L^2/6 = 37011.0;  exact orbits = 18604;  2*orbits = 37208
  L=1000: DD 2 pi A(F) L^2 = 1644934.1;  AD (3.11) integrated = 1644934.1;  pi^2L^2/6 = 1644934.1;  exact orbits = 823081;  2*orbits = 1646162
  L=3000: DD 2 pi A(F) L^2 = 14804406.6;  AD (3.11) integrated = 14804406.6;  pi^2L^2/6 = 14804406.6;  exact orbits = 7405170;  2*orbits = 14810340

VERDICT: AD's exact count explicitly multiplies by 2 for a1<0 (i.e. counts N and -N as distinct),
and that is what the continuum density integrated over F reproduces.  Modulo the full SL(2,Z),
which contains -1: (A,B) -> (-A,-B) at fixed tau, the count is sum sigma ~ pi^2 L^2/12.
